# The deploy root is the repository root, not frontend/, because the build reads
# the signed captures out of contract/fixtures/ — see frontend/fixtures.ts and
# the hallmarkFixtures plugin in vite.config.ts. So only the things the build
# cannot possibly need are excluded, and target/ is the one that matters: it is
# 2.4 GB of Rust artifacts and on its own pushes the upload past Vercel's
# 15,000-file limit.
#
# contract/ is NOT excluded. Excluding a directory and re-including a child of
# it does not work in this format, and contract/fixtures/ is load-bearing.
#
# The patterns are anchored, so `target/` alone matches only the workspace
# target at the root and silently leaves contract/target — another 1.0 GB —
# in the upload. That failed as `write EPIPE` partway through 1.1 GB, which
# reads like a network fault and is not. Both spellings, deliberately.
target/
**/target/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.git/
frontend/dist/
.DS_Store
